WEBVTT

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:06.020
Toys. They are miraculous buds that swell from the hearts of the chosen.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:12.490
Some flowers are born pure, while others bloom laced with poison.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.440
The Age of Detectives.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.660
The two flowers, vying for beauty.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:24.460
Their names are the Detective and the Phantom Thief.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:12.020
Itadakimasu!

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:19.200
I-Is it really all right to eat all this?

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:23.910
Of course. I made it all for you.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.910
Thanks!

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:29.280
So why's Nezu here?

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.600
I guided this kid all the way here! Can't you see anything but the food?!

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:35.090
Well then, you can have some too, Nezu-kun!

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.380
It's fine, I'm heading home anyways.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.170
Doesn't look like it...

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:43.610
We're celebrating today, so the more people, the merrier!

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:44.870
Isn't that right?

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:48.020
If that's what Sherlock-senpai says, then please join us.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:53.610
F-Fine... A little, I guess.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.850
So what exactly are we celebrating here?

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.420
Um, well...

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:13.410
A one year anniversary since Sherlock-senpai and I met.

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:16.800
That's it! We met in a Toys class, didn't we?

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:17.790
That's right.

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:19.760
You celebrate such a trivial thing?

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:24.560
I admire Sherlock-senpai for her stoutness and excellence.

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.510
What's that?

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:34.630
It's a Ouija board...

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:35.840
Edible?

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:39.240
Well, it answers any question you ask it.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:42.490
Really?!

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:48.370
Well then, please put a finger on this <i>planchette</i>, and then close your eyes.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:53.620
Please tell us... Will our Toys return to us soon?

00:03:57.590 --> 00:03:58.780
They will!

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.010
Yay!

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.880
You guys moved it to "Yes" on purpose, didn't you?

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.450
Of course not!

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:07.320
No way!

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:12.640
Well then, ask it who's the stupidest amongst yourselves!

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.070
Thought so.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:31.660
Stop it! Let's ask another question!

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:35.000
Who's the super meanest in this academy?!

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:38.420
"N, E, Z, U..."

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.030
Nezu!

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:41.750
As I thought!

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:43.920
You little...!

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:45.780
Just as I thought, <i>you're</i> the super meanest here!

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:56.280
Thank you very much for walking me to the dorms.

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:59.940
It's nothing. It's late, and I'm not as mean as they say, so...

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:04.000
Here, my thanks. Though it's not much.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.760
Huh? Well, I didn't expect anything, but...

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:12.880
It's not what you think!

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:17.920
Not bad...

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:38.450
Well, next up is some warning advice when riding a bicycle.

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:40.020
Tell us, Poporo-kun.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:44.760
"When it gets dark, make sure you put on some reflectors, or else a car will crash into you."

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.640
Poporo-kun's really got a dirty mouth, eh?

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:51.530
"I hate detectives, so I'm gonna go home."

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:54.570
And that's it for the Road Safety Classroom.

00:05:55.990 --> 00:06:00.290
It's amazing that the puppet and Kokoro-chan sound so much alike!

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:03.920
Is that so? We're of the same flesh, so...

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:08.120
"Like hell we are! Just shut up and listen to the lesson!! And..."

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:10.970
Don't call me Kokoro-chan, you dimwit!!

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:19.260
Jeez... why do I, Akechi Kokoro, with an IQ of 13 billion, have to do this shabby job?

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:27.990
What are those? Invitations for Milky Holmes?

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:40.170
Dying message...

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:45.930
Nezu-kun!

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:48.270
Is it true?

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:53.640
Milky Holmes. You are the ones who would know best.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.640
What do you mean?

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:59.350
The last letters that Nezu-san wrote.

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:02.440
"M.H." In other words, "Milky Holmes."

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:08.160
Therefore, you are the ones that killed Nezu-san.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:09.110
No way!

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:11.530
You're completely wrong!

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.870
We're shocked enough from this incident as it is, yet now...

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:16.050
This is cruel! It's a false accusation!

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:19.160
Well then, how would you explain this?

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:21.040
Henriette-san!

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:25.420
It wasn't us! Please believe us!!

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:29.920
If you really are innocent, then prove it by tomorrow morning.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:33.590
If not, then I shall hand you over to the police.

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:39.800
What should we do?

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:41.580
Don't ask me...

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:44.160
We're gonna get criminal records...

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:45.730
Please wait!

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:48.020
It's not like we've been judged guilty yet!

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:50.520
We're going to infer who the real criminal is!

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:52.990
We can do it without our Toys!

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:59.700
As expected of Arsène-sama. She actually cornered Milky Holmes that far...

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:00.670
Yes!

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:03.580
Arsène-sama is the ruthless queen of the night.

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:10.550
Even though you said that, we only have this picture as our clue! What'll we do?

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.080
Well...

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:13.230
We'll do our best!

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:17.890
That's impossible. Our ancestors might have been able to infer much quicker,

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.740
but as for us...

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:25.630
Well, if we ask our ancestors through this...

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:27.520
Herc-san, that's it!

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:32.440
Holmes-san, Holmes-san...

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:33.990
Gray-san, Gray-san...

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:35.680
Wolfe-san, Wolfe-san...

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:37.460
Poirot-san...

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:42.200
Please infer who the real criminal is!

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:21.160
Everyone! Are you okay?

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:25.360
Yes, I shall infer for you.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:28.250
With my little gray cells, that is.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:36.260
The one solving this case shall be me. A detective is a suiting job for a woman, after all.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:40.720
But before that, bring me some caviar for now.

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:45.930
Um.. what's happened to everyone?

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:51.410
Oh, how rude of me. I am the great detective, Hercule Poirot.

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:53.970
Great detective, Cordelia Gray.

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:56.110
Great detective, Nero Wolfe.

00:09:56.720 --> 00:10:01.870
Ehh?! Everyone's... ancestors?!

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:15.840
Huh? Boys' Love Bull Session?!

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.490
No, Toys of Possession!

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:24.000
Poirot-san said that their consciousnesses were trapped inside the Ouija board with that Toys...

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:26.600
But now, their spirits are free!

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:30.060
So hungry...

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:33.660
I see. I understand the situation.

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:35.900
We understand, but...

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:38.780
Can we really trust anything this baldy says?

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:43.970
Oh my, is this how far Holmes Detective Academy has fallen?

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:48.250
At Poirot Detective Academy, we wouldn't have stupid students like you running around!

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:54.040
Akechi-san is a policeman, mister.

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:57.550
Police? Ah, that must be why she's stupid.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:01.990
Hey!! I'll arrest you for defaming me!

00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:05.680
Also, being told that by you really pisses me off!

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.930
Please stop...

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:09.470
What's that?

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:11.570
You children should go to bed now.

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:14.560
Yes. Good night! Or else your Mama shall be mad at you!

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:16.570
That's what they say, Kokoro-chan!

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.780
Don't say that!

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.280
Why me?

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:22.120
At any rate...

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:26.200
If you're going to prove Milky Holmes' innocence, please do it right away.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:31.390
My, my. Well then, I shall start.

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:33.420
We're counting on you, Nero's grandfather!

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:37.770
Leave it to me. This case is nothing but child's play to me.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:44.140
Everyone, how about thinking that this message was actually part of a picture?

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:47.640
Oh, <i>how</i> smart! And how exactly does that help us?!

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:50.480
This!

00:11:51.450 --> 00:11:52.480
Kimura-san?

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:54.310
Who the heck is that?!

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:55.190
Looks like a monkey.

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:58.570
Indeed! The culprit is a monkey in the academy!

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:00.260
There are no monkeys within this academy.

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:02.880
Oh, right... They usually aren't, eh...

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:04.620
Hey, you geezer!

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:07.410
Next person, please!

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:11.360
My turn next.

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:14.010
Cordelia-san's grandmother, fight!

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:15.310
Leave it to me.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:21.030
Why does everyone think that you read the message this way?

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:22.320
Yes, for example...

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:25.070
Look at it this way.

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:34.870
And then two eyes, whiskers, this way and that, and you get...!

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:36.510
Uh, what's that?

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:37.810
A hamster.

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.320
What, a drawing song?!

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:42.320
Well then, next person, please.

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:45.160
Time for the winner to make his appearance!

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:47.450
Herc-san's grandfather, if you would!

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:52.940
Gray does have a point about that picture.

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:56.420
The message is certainly not limited to one way of reading only.

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:58.080
In that case...

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:02.460
If you align it this way, the image of the real criminal should come to mind.

00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:05.430
The culprit is amongst one of us!

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:08.390
That's because it's Milky Holmes!

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:11.120
The <i>katakana</i> for "E," エ...

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:12.600
The <i>hiragana</i> for "Ro," ろ...

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:14.650
So that means the culprit is...

00:13:14.650 --> 00:13:16.980
...actually a very erotic lady!

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:19.940
What's the meaning of this?

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:23.880
What the hell are you saying?! <i>You're</i> the criminal, dammit!

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:28.450
Hamsters committing murder? Idiot.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:30.870
Hamsters are cuter than monkeys!

00:13:32.090 --> 00:13:35.200
Are these people really great detectives?

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:36.750
They should be, but...

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:39.620
Um...

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:42.340
What? Did you think up another drawing song?

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:47.090
That's not it. As Poirot-san said, if you read it horizontally...

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:52.140
Can't you read this as a "3"?

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:56.770
Eh? Anybody could guess that! So what are you getting at?

00:13:58.330 --> 00:13:59.650
Um...

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:02.670
You are totally useless!

00:14:12.020 --> 00:14:13.460
W-What's that?!

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:16.150
It's the bronze statue of my ancestor!

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:22.840
Sherlock!

00:14:32.110 --> 00:14:34.430
Sherlock, are you unhurt?

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:37.890
A foolish question, Watson-kun.

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:42.150
Sherlock?

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:48.150
Could you be Grandpa Holmes?

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:50.870
A fine observation.

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:53.090
Where were you loitering about?

00:14:53.090 --> 00:14:58.240
We thought we'd give you the final word on this, so we made joke inferences while we waited.

00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:03.040
Sorry about that. I possessed my own bronze statue by mistake.

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:08.550
Sherlock Holmes. If even you are joking around, then I shall take my leave.

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:13.850
Don't be so hasty, Watson-kun. After all,
I've already figured out who the real criminal is.

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:17.720
Ooh, really?

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:22.000
When the victim first met the criminal,
the victim didn't know the criminal's name.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:25.520
There was a possibility that the victim tried to ask the criminal, but it didn't go over too well.

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:27.690
And then, a tragedy happened.

00:15:30.210 --> 00:15:33.700
The only things that the victim could remember about the criminal were a couple of numerals.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:38.220
Ah, so maybe the 3 means the third dormitory building?

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:41.950
Yes. And this is the roman numeral I.

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:45.810
This academy dorm's first block, third building.

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:47.550
In other words, <i>you.</i>

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:55.800
Sonia-chan?!

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:05.270
The cat's outta the bag now...

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.380
Who... are you?

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:16.290
Like I said, Sherlock Holmes...

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:18.200
Miss Phantom Thief.

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:22.530
Oops, I've gotta run after her.

00:16:22.530 --> 00:16:25.710
She's the one that needs saving right now.

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:33.880
You're being unreasonably stubborn. Just give yourself up.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:35.150
Shut up!

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:42.350
Damn!

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:56.910
Ah, Kamaboko!

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:08.080
I did it!

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:12.450
I guess I really am...

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:13.720
...a bully!

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:20.510
Sonia-chan!

00:17:42.570 --> 00:17:45.140
Suspect secured, Watson-kun.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.000
We did it!

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:52.500
His Toys is amazing...

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:55.980
He's boosted his telekinesis to its utmost limits, huh?

00:17:57.200 --> 00:18:02.510
I'd like a showdown with him someday.
The winner in beauty shall be me, though.

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:05.360
So you don't need to play dead anymore?

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:07.890
Arsène-sama said it's fine now.

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:13.360
So that's... Holmes' lineage...

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:18.300
Sherlock.

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:22.180
No, Mister Holmes. I thank you.

00:18:22.180 --> 00:18:24.850
Oh, it was nothing, miss.

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:26.830
Well then...

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:31.090
Let's go back to where we came from, brethren?

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:33.850
Sounds good. I'm hungry, anyways.

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:35.740
It's no fun without a case to solve.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:38.350
Well, it was a great way to spend time.

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:42.180
Everyone!

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:46.350
We'll leave these kids in your care, miss.

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:47.730
See ya!

00:18:52.970 --> 00:18:54.820
Everyone, are you okay?

00:18:58.050 --> 00:19:00.600
Hey, what was Sherlock's Toys?

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:02.600
It was amazing!

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:06.170
But who was he chasing?

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:08.020
Good question...

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:16.920
"Your Toys shall return after a great test..."

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:19.170
A message from our grandparents!

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:21.800
I see! So our Toys really are gonna return!

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:23.040
Thank goodness!

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:30.350
It was all an act, wasn't it?

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:35.070
Your aim was to get Milky Holmes to solve this case,

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:40.320
so that they would earn back the respect they had gathered in the past.

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:44.680
The one who left that message for them was not the victim, but rather, you.

00:19:44.680 --> 00:19:52.000
Since Milky Holmes thought they were being doubted, they went out to solve this case, whether they were willing to or not.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.400
Am I correct?

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:55.480
How did you...?

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:58.240
Because I would've done the same.

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:05.200
Anyways, having caused an incident of this scale, I cannot permit you to remain in this academy.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:08.470
Yes. I'm prepared for the consequences. Is it expulsion?

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:12.690
A letter of recommendation.

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:15.480
Start over at Poirot Detective Academy.

00:20:16.070 --> 00:20:21.200
You should not waste your Toys. What you should become is a detective.

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:23.290
Not a phantom thief.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:25.720
Yes!

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:30.240
Eh? Sonia-chan transferred?

00:20:30.240 --> 00:20:33.400
I heard about that just earlier, too. It surprised me!

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:35.420
It'll be lonely from now on...

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:37.940
She can't give us food anymore, huh?

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:41.710
We'll meet her again because we're all detectives!

00:20:41.710 --> 00:20:42.760
But...

00:20:43.330 --> 00:20:46.760
We won't ever see Nezu-kun again, huh?

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:51.460
Nezu-kun, Nezu-kun, can you hear us?

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:55.470
Nezu-kun turned into a star, but we'll never forget about him!

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:58.030
Where is he right now?

00:20:58.030 --> 00:21:00.400
In the first level of hell? The second?

00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:04.200
Huh? What, what?

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:04.990
What is this?

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:06.030
What?!

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:17.380
What're you doing?

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:19.810
Whoa, Nezu!

00:21:19.810 --> 00:21:21.020
Nezu-kun!

00:21:21.020 --> 00:21:22.630
So you turned into a ghost and came to visit us, eh?

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:25.280
Eh? I'm alive!

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:28.830
Nezu-kun will live on forever in our hearts!

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:30.510
May he rest in peace.

00:21:31.190 --> 00:21:33.390
I hope you find happiness there!

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:35.600
Please watch over us.

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:39.270
AS IF!!

00:23:19.880 --> 00:23:21.470
I see, that's true.

00:23:21.470 --> 00:23:23.730
Though they may have borrowed their ancestors' powers,

00:23:23.730 --> 00:23:26.600
Sherlock's Toys's potential ability is quite menacing.

00:23:29.520 --> 00:23:32.930
We must drive Milky Holmes out at all costs.

00:23:32.930 --> 00:23:35.630
Being detectives doesn't even suit them in the first place.

00:23:37.490 --> 00:23:41.410
Ahh, right! By the way, what have you been saying?

00:23:41.410 --> 00:23:44.270
Next time: An Unsuitable Job for Milky Holmes.

00:23:45.230 --> 00:23:47.780
What? You're the culprit?!
